  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    Kaggle has no API for notebook Secrets, so the tunnel credentials (and a git deploy key, if you set one) are stored in the private notebook's
    source, readable by anyone with Can Edit on it. Understand that before you share a workspace. Report vulnerabilities privately, as the
    <a href={links.security}>security policy</a> describes.
  </p>

